  "notes": "Source: official UA-PTC 2025-2026 Academic Catalog graduation map (poid=1488), transcribed 2026-10-01. FULL-TIME COHORT of the AAS in Health Information Technology (companion part-time cohort map poid=1489 seeded separately). Two-year degree; all HIMT courses are offered ONLINE with the exception of clinical courses. Accredited by the Commission on Accreditation for Health Informatics and Information Management Education (CAHIIM). Class size limited to 25 students per cohort; selective admissions process. To apply: https://uaptc.edu/health-info-tech/application; application must be received by July 1st for Fall entrance. Applicants must have completed all 22 hours of General Education courses before admission; minimum cumulative GPA of 2.25 required. All HIMT courses must be completed with a grade of C or better. Degree requires 60 credit hours. Term sums: 13+9+12+12+2+12 = 60 (consistent with printed total). The Spring - HIT Semester Two term prints no term total (listed sum 12). Renamed 2026-10-01 with -full-time suffix to distinguish the part-time cohort variant; content matches the prior seed.",
